# Static files and add-on extraction

- `internal/staticfiles.Store` owns `datadir.Layout.Static()`. Names are allowlisted by `ValidateName` (no Windows device names, no trailing dot) and resolved inside the directory; invalid names are rejected, never rewritten. Uploads go through `Stage` (temp file `.upload-*` in the same directory, size-limited, fsynced) and `Commit` (hard link for no-overwrite, rename for `replace`; all files of one request or none). `Open` removes stale temporaries. Never buffer whole uploads in memory; the HTTP handler streams multipart parts and reads the raw `filename` parameter (not `Part.FileName`, which strips directories).
- `internal/extract.Zip(zipPath, tmpRoot, Limits)` is the only extractor (ZIP only, no tar). It validates the whole central directory first (entry count, sizes, compression ratio, depth, path length, unsafe or colliding names including case-insensitive collisions, non-regular entries), creates its own fresh `os.MkdirTemp` destination under `tmpRoot` (use `datadir.Layout.Tmp()`), masks modes to 0644/0755 and enforces sizes again while copying. Never extract into an existing tree such as a repository checkout. It has no HTTP caller yet; the build pipeline will use it.
- Verify with `go test ./internal/staticfiles/... ./internal/extract/...` (bombs, traversal, modes, concurrent and interrupted uploads are covered).
